<subpara id="RM0000008Y100ZX_04" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D8L00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the SPD line branches to other ECUs from an option connector, etc., first disconnect those circuits and inspect.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), read the Freeze Frame Data. Freeze Frame Data records part of the engine operating conditions when a malfunction occurs, and this information is useful for troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000008Y100ZX_03" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000008Y100ZX_03_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D8H00000">
<scantool type="4"/>
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (Vehicle Speed)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the speedometer operates normally.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test of the vehicle.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, read the Data List item [Vehicle Speed] from [ECU Data Monitor].</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>SST (TaSCAN) data monitor display and speedometer display are the same</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000008Y100ZX_03_0013" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000008Y100ZX_03_0014" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000008Y100ZX_03_0013">
<testtitle>Inspection for Intermittent Problems<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000CD101YX"/>
</testtitle>
